\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4}{\ignorespaces The dark noise of the FD10D at different reverse biases. The maximum datasheet value is 1.8V, above this voltage electrons can start tunnelling across the band gap. The rolling off above \SIunits {9}{\tmspace  +\thinmuskip {.1667em}kHz} is an artefact of the circuit. Above 0.65\tmspace  +\thinmuskip {.1667em}V reverse bias, the $1/f$ noise becomes larger than shot noise. At this reverse bias, the quantum efficiency is $\sim $70\%. These measurements were made at room temperature.\relax }}{7}}
\newlabel{fig:fd10ddarknoisereversebias}{{4}{7}}
